ana: quick sync — i'm rewriting the troubleshooting entry for the case where apps see a partial generated response because of a 429 that arrives mid-stream + context-trim fallback. pushed a draft to PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4567. can folks weigh in on the SDK snippet we should show?
ryan: linked — skimmed. i'd prefer a tiny typescript snippet that shows: detect 429, retry with backoff, and if still failing, send a trimmed prompt (prefix-preserve) and then stitch responses. keep it <10 lines.
sam: agree. also add a note about how KV/prefix caching may make stitching tricky — mention invalidation header we added last quarter.
maria: question — what is the SDK default retry behaviour? do we need to call into the SDK retry helper or show manual fetch+retry?
ana (ana): the SDK exposes retry helpers but they don't auto-trim. i think example should use SDK.retryWithBackoff + simple trim util to illustrate pattern. readers can then drop into the higher-level helper.
ryan: ok. i'll draft a TS snippet. quick idea: show try { client.generate(...) } catch(err) { if err.code==429) { await backoff(); // retry once; then if still 429, trimContextAndRetry() } } and show tiny trim function. keep comments short.
sam: can you include the header check for "x-cache-invalidate" so folks remember to clear the prefix cache when stitching?
ryan: done in draft below. please nitpick.
```
// typescript (for docs snippet)
try {
  const res = await client.generate({ model: 'rwd-small-v1', prompt: longPrompt });
  return res;
} catch (err) {
  if (err.code === 429) {
    await sdk.helpers.backoff(2); // retry once
    try { return await client.generate({ model: 'rwd-small-v1', prompt: longPrompt }); } catch (err2) {
      if (err2.code === 429) {
        // last-resort: trim oldest context, preserve system/prefix
        const trimmed = trimContext(longPrompt, { preservePrefixLines: 2 });
        const r = await client.generate({ model: 'rwd-small-v1', prompt: trimmed });
        // if backend returns cache-invalidate header, clear local prefix cache
        if (r.headers?.['x-cache-invalidate']) cache.clearPrefix(longPrompt.prefixId);
        return stitchResponses(r, /* originalPrompt */ longPrompt);
      }
      throw err2;
    }
  }
  throw err;
}

function trimContext(prompt: string, opts = { preservePrefixLines: 1 }) {
  // simple example: drop N earliest user turns
  const lines = prompt.split('\n');
  const keep = Math.max(1, lines.length - (opts.preservePrefixLines + 50));
  return lines.slice(keep).join('\n');
}
```
